    {
      "id": "kpk1-l07-a3-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l07-a3-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Biernik of people and animals"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "For a man, a boy or an animal, a masculine noun takes *-a* in the accusative, and its adjective *-ego*: *mam inteligentnego brata*, *mam małego kota*. A man's word in *-a* changes like a feminine one: *mam dobrego tatę*. Ask *kogo?* for a person or an animal and *co?* for a thing."
      },
      "table": {
        "title": {
          "en": "Biernik: kogo?"
        },
        "columns": [
          {
            "header": "brat"
          },
          {
